@ Index:   Compute factorial recursively
@ Author:  Walter Bonin
@ Created: Original publication date unknown
@ Version: 3.1
@ Tested:  3 returns 6, 5 returns 120, 1 returns 1, 0 returns 1.
@ Input:   X = 3 (also 5, 1, 0)
@ Output:  X = 6 (5 returns 120, 1 returns 1, 0 returns 1)
@
@ Originally published in Appendix B of the WP34s Manual as a recursive programming demo called FACT.
@
@ Usage is the same as the built-in 𝑥! operation: input value in X,
@ factorial of same output in X; stack-neutral for inputs > 1.
@
@ The result is valid for X ≥ 0 inputs only.  Whereas the fact-iter
@ implementation diagnoses the X<0 error case, this one incorrectly
@ returns 1 for negative inputs.
LBL ‘FactRec’
  IP
  𝑥>? 1.
    GTO 00
  1.
  RTN

LBL 00
  LocR 01
  STO R.00
  DECR X
  XEQ ‘FactRec’
  RCL× R.00
  RTN
  END
